    <string name="a11y_explain_title">What Syncliko can see</string>
    <string name="a11y_explain_body">Android warns that accessibility apps can see your screen and control the phone. Syncliko only listens for the moment you tap “Copy” or a “Copied” message appears, then reads the clipboard. It doesn’t read text on screen, doesn’t tap anything, and sends data only to your Mac.</string>
    <string name="a11y_step_restricted">App info → ⋮ → Allow restricted settings</string>
    <string name="a11y_step_enable">Accessibility → Installed apps → Syncliko automatic sending → On</string>
    <string name="a11y_stalled">Android stopped the service. Turn it off and on again in Accessibility settings.</string>
    <string name="toast_note">Android shows “Syncliko pasted from your clipboard” each time a copy is sent. That’s expected.</string>
